cal-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-4-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;New Media Theory Course\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Requirement in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">New Media Theory Course</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-4-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Advanced Analysis III\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Requirement in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Advanced Analysis III</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-4-4-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Advanced Analysis II\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Requirement in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Advanced Analysis II</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">17 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-spring\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 3</span><span class=\"col-term\">Spring</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-5-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;UB Curriculum Capstone&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;UB Curriculum Capstone (UBC 399) is the culminating general education requirement. It is a one-credit course in which you will work in UBPortfolio, with the support of your Capstone instructor, to create a reflective and integrative Capstone ePortfolio based on your UB Curriculum coursework and lived experiences outside of the classroom. All UB Curriculum courses must be completed or in-progress to enroll in and complete UBC 399. Students who drop an in-progress course will be removed from UBC 399 through the add/drop period. Students who resign an in-progress course may not be able to successfully complete the Capstone.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;1&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;All UB Curriculum courses must be completed or in-progress to enroll in and complete UBC 399. UB Seminar is a prerequisite to UBC 399 and therefore cannot be taken concurrently. If you enrolled today in your remaining UBC course(s), HUB will allow you to enroll tomorrow. For questions, email: ubcurriculum@buffalo.edu.&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: true}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">UBC 399MNT</span><span class=\"box-title\">UB Curriculum Capstone</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">1 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-5-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Media and Culture Course\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Requirement in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Media and Culture Course</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-5-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_elective&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Elective\\&quot; is an elective slot specific to this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a UB Curriculum-wide component - the exact eligible courses depend on this program&#x27;s requirements as listed in the Undergraduate Catalog.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Elective in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Elective</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-5-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_elective&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Elective\\&quot; is an elective slot specific to this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a UB Curriculum-wide component - the exact eligible courses depend on this program&#x27;s requirements as listed in the Undergraduate Catalog.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Elective in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Elective</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-5-4-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Advanced Analysis IV\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Requirement in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Advanced Analysis IV</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">15 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-fall\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 4</span><span class=\"col-term\">Fall</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-6-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Marketing Arts &amp; Culture Sect&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course teaches the skills and knowledge to develop an effective marketing strategy for an arts organization. Students learn how to do market research, develop a marketing plan for various organizational purposes including promoting events, performances, and exhibits, as well as for fundraising, donor development, increasing memberships, and for good public relations in a community.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: null, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: null, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">AAP 552LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Arts Marketing and Analysis</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-6-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Leadership &amp; Finance in Arts&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Good financial management ensures the stability, longevity, and sustainability of an arts organization. The focus of this course is on how basic financial principles and leadership skills contribute to sound decision making and management of arts enterprises, with special focus on nonprofits. Students will become familiar with the use of financial practices, day-to-day financial activities, financial documents, as well as the vocabulary needed for carrying out financial functions and for leading staff and board members towards responsible financial decision making in the arts nonprofit sector. The focus is on active learning modalities and applications coupled with important historical and theoretical contexts.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: null, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: null, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">AAP 551LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Arts Business and Finance</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-6-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Managing Arts in 21st Century&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Leading and managing arts and cultural organizations in today\\u2019s world means balancing organizational needs against those of the community and the artists served. This course focuses on the skills and knowledge to carry out the functions of leading and managing resources (personnel, finances, property) for effective management of arts and culture enterprises. Students are introduced to key social, political, legal, ethical, and economic forces affecting arts and culture, while also acquiring basic skills in the functions of running a successful and sustainable organization. Skills learned include appropriate use of AI and other technologies for arts management purposes.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: null, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: null, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">AAP 501SEM</span><span class=\"box-title\">Why Manage the Arts?</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-6-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_elective&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;DMS Elective\\&quot; is an elective slot specific to this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a UB Curriculum-wide component - the exact eligible courses depend on this program&#x27;s requirements as listed in the Undergraduate Catalog.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Elective in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">DMS Elective</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-6-4-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_elective&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;DMS Elective\\&quot; is an elective slot specific to this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a UB Curriculum-wide component - the exact eligible courses depend on this program&#x27;s requirements as listed in the Undergraduate Catalog.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Elective in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">DMS Elective</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">17 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-spring\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 4</span><span class=\"col-term\">Spring</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-7-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Research for Arts Leaders&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Research is fundamental to effective arts leadership and cultural management. Whether writing grants, developing strategic plans, evaluating programs, understanding audiences, or making evidence-based decisions, cultural managers rely on research skills daily. Leaders in the cultural sector must also engage with academic research to understand trends, challenges, and opportunities in the field. This course equips students with conceptual and practical research skills for cultural management contexts. Students learn to formulate research questions, design research protocols, select appropriate methods, conduct ethical research, and communicate findings effectively. The course emphasizes practical applications of research in arts/cultural organizations and integrates appropriate use of artificial intelligence tools throughout the research process\\u2013from literature review and data collection to analysis and presentation. The course also covers use of assistive AI in research and data analysis.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: null, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: null, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">AAP 509SEM</span><span class=\"box-title\">Research in Arts Mgmt</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-7-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Law for Arts &amp; Cultural Ldrshp&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Art law is the body of law, involving numerous disciplines, that protects, regulates and facilitates the creation, use and marketing of art. Art law is closely related to, and often overlaps with, cultural property law. This course provides knowledge of concepts of legal reasoning and contemporary law in order to familiarize students with the history and impact of seminal cases and court decisions on art making, exhibition, performance, transfer of ownership, artists\\u2019 rights, copyright, nonprofit law, contracts, and other pertinent legal issues. The course covers local, national, and international cases of importance with emphasis on applying knowledge to an arts leadership and cultural management context.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: null, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: null, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">AAP 585SEM</span><span class=\"box-title\">Legal Issues in Arts Mgmt</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-7-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Fieldwork in Arts Mgmt&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course is designed to provide students with the opportunity to learn about the professional environment and to bring together the theory and practice of arts management. It is intended to prepare students for their future careers as arts managers. Students will be teamed with a professional arts, cultural, or advocacy organization on a specific project. These projects are designed in consultation between the Program, the course instructor and the participating organization. The projects selected will have clearly defined objectives and goals.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: null, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: null, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">AAP 511TUT</span><span class=\"box-title\">Fieldwork in Arts Mgmt</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-7-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_elective&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;AAP Elective\\&quot; is an elective slot specific to this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a UB Curriculum-wide component - the exact eligible courses depend on this program&#x27;s requirements as listed in the Undergraduate Catalog.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Elective in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">AAP Elective</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">12 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-fall\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 5</span><span class=\"col-term\">Fall</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-8-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_elective&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;AAP Elective\\&quot; is an elective slot specific to this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a UB Curriculum-wide component - the exact eligible courses depend on this program&#x27;s requirements as listed in the Undergraduate Catalog.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Elective in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">AAP Elective</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-8-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Cultural Policy Values and Per&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Cultural policies are the ways governments make the arts happen through laws, regulations, financial support, programs, information and a variety of other means. Public policies reflect the intentions, values, and aims of citizens expressed through government initiatives. In this course, students will learn how policy is made and how it works(and sometimes doesn?t work) to ensure that artists can make art, and that the public can participate in the arts in all its forms. Topics include the policy process, rights of artists and citizens, historical and current controversies impacting on the arts, the role of arts organizations, civic engagement, and how individuals can participate in the policy process through advocacy and other means. While the focus is on US cultural policy, students also acquire knowledge about cultural policies globally and internationally.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: null, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: null, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">AAP 508SEM</span><span class=\"box-title\">Arts/Cul Pol &amp; Diplomacy</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-8-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Managing Arts &amp; Cultural Facil&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;A well-managed arts or cultural space is not merely a container for art and cultural activities, but an active agent in fulfilling an organization\\u2019s mission, shaping audience experience, and fostering community engagement. This course positions the arts facility as a central system in the cultural ecosystem, requiring a manager who can think holistically while maintaining a well-running arts or cultural facility, introducing students to systems-level leadership balanced with practical, day-to-day skills of running a safe and welcoming arts and cultural facility. Students learn to navigate complex regulatory environments, local permitting processes, and accessibility standards, while building effective relationships with local government officials, community organizations, and cultural partners. Key topics include the development of internal policies and procedures; strategic scheduling and comprehensive human resource management; the arts/cultural facility as a hospitality site; working effectively with diverse personnel including union and non-union staff; the design of effective wayfinding systems; comprehensive security, safety, and risk management protocols; effective practices for working with artists and the public; targeted marketing for arts venues; understanding and obtaining local permits and licenses; building collaborative relationships with municipal agencies and community groups; and the growing importance of environmental and sustainability issues in the cultural sector, as well as integration of AI tools for facilities management.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: null, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: null, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">AAP 560TUT</span><span class=\"box-title\">Managing Arts Spaces</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-8-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_elective&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;AAP Elective\\&quot; is an elective slot specific to this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a UB Curriculum-wide component - the exact eligible courses depend on this program&#x27;s requirements as listed in the Undergraduate Catalog.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Elective in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">AAP Elective</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">12 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-spring\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 5</span><span class=\"col-term\">Spring</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-9-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Cultural Management Project&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;The project course combines the student?s knowledge and skills for completing the culminating project for the MA Arts Management Degree. Students will have the opportunity for intensive review of research skills for a defined arts management problem leading to design and planning of a project to address the problem. Students will also learn appropriate and ethical uses of AI for research purposes and how to apply course learning into a viable project. Students receive weekly guidance from the instructor and peer feedback on written work and oral presentations.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;1-3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: null, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: null, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: true, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;, &quot;groups&quot;: [{&quot;requirement_type&quot;: &quot;choice_required&quot;, &quot;group&quot;: &quot;Final Project or Thesis Guidance (choose 1 of 2)&quot;, &quot;courses&quot;: [{&quot;code&quot;: &quot;AAP 512&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Final Project or Thesis Guidance&quot;}, {&quot;code&quot;: &quot;AAP 513&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Final Project or Thesis Guidance&quot;}]}]}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">full list on click</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Final Project or Thesis Guidance (choose 1 of 2)</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"media-study-ba-critical-studies-concentration-arts-management-ma__box-9-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_elective&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;AAP Elective\\&quot; is an elective slot specific to this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a UB Curriculum-wide component - the exact eligible courses depend on this program&#x27;s requirements as listed in the Undergraduate Catalog.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=8200&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" r